+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates tool call arguments against the registered tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, returning schema failures as a `ToolResponse` so the AI model can self-correct within the existing tool-round budget instead of aborting the session with a transport error.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor, rejecting missing required fields, wrong-typed fields, and disallowed enum values with a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property path and constraint without invoking the executor or leaking offending input values into the result or logs ([validated by: rejects missing required, wrong-typed, and disallowed-enum input before calling the executor without leaking offending values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only: valid input carrying unlisted extra properties and omitted defaulted fields passes through to the executor unmodified, while uncoerced type mismatches are rejected ([validated by: passes valid input with unlisted properties and omitted defaulted fields through unmodified while rejecting uncoerced type mismatches](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L64)).
+- Calling `ToolRegistry.execute` with an unregistered tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` rather than returning a `ToolResponse`.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time; an uncompilable schema causes `register` to throw synchronously with an error message naming the tool ([validated by: throws synchronously at register time for an uncompilable inputSchema and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
+- A static tool's compiled validator is reused across repeated `execute` calls rather than recompiling per call.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves and validates against the schema returned for each `execute` call rather than a stale cached schema ([validated by: validates a function-valued ToolDefinitionSource against the schema returned on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L100)).
+
+## Orchestrator retry loop
+
+- When schema validation rejects a tool call during a conversation turn, `chatOrchestrator` passes the rejection `ToolResponse` back to the provider on the next round so the model can retry with valid input and `processMessage` resolves ([validated by: returns schema rejection to the model so it can retry with valid input and resolve](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L10)).
